that address differences with the US about Tehran's nuclear program.\n\nThe development is raising hopes that the two 
sides could be inching toward indirect talks on one of the thorniest issues that Mr Trump says must be resolved as 
part of any deal meant to end the more than eight-month-old war.\n\nBut one of the officials stressed that the 
Iranians remained unwilling to engage in negotiations with the Trump administration over its atomic activities until 
