attack\n\nAt least three people have been injured in the city and the surrounding region. Damage has been reported at 
homes, apartment buildings, and a kindergarten.\n\nActual Article Body:\nEditor's Note: This is a developing story and 
is being updated.\n\nSeveral waves of Russian ballistic missiles hit Kyiv overnight on Nov. 6-7, just hours after 
President Volodymyr Zelensky warned that Russia was preparing another large-scale infrastructure attack.\n\nAt least 
two people in the city of Kyiv have been wounded, along with a third victim in the surrounding region, according to 
authorities.\n\nAs Ukraine's Air Force warned that ballistic missiles were bound for the capital, a series of 
explosions rocked the city, according to Kyiv Independent journalists on the ground.\n\nThe first barrage of missiles 
