published in the journal Nursing Research, evaluated 196 adults diagnosed with prediabetes who routinely logged fewer 
than 6.5 hours of sleep nightly. Half the group took part in an eight-week lifestyle education course on diet, 
exercise and stress.\n\nGoing to bed earlier was linked to weight loss in adults with prediabetes, independent of the 
total number of hours they spent asleep. (iStock)\n\nThe other half received the same training alongside behavioral 
coaching meant to get them to go to bed earlier in gradual phases.\n\nDIETITIAN REVEALS SIMPLE EATING STRATEGY FOR 
